From: Rizki Ramadhan <achmadrizkiramadhan0101@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uwe5622: select the radio_idx set_wiphy_params prototype on backports

cfg80211 grew a radio_idx argument for set_wiphy_params in 6.17, and the
driver already carries both prototypes. OpenWrt backports that API onto
older target kernels, so on a 6.12 target the kernel version test picks the
old prototype while the backported header declares the new one:

  error: initialization of 'int (*)(struct wiphy *, int, u32)' from
  incompatible pointer type 'int (*)(struct wiphy *, u32)'

Extend the guard with OPENWRT_CFG80211_BACKPORT, the same way the
change_beacon prototype is already selected.

Signed-off-by: Rizki Ramadhan <achmadrizkiramadhan0101@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
index 61be02f..bd6e7a4 100644
--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -2328,7 +2328,8 @@ err:
 	return ret;
 }
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 17, 0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 17, 0) || \
+	defined(OPENWRT_CFG80211_BACKPORT)
 static int sprdwl_cfg80211_set_wiphy_params(struct wiphy *wiphy, int radio_idx, u32 changed)
 #else
 static int sprdwl_cfg80211_set_wiphy_params(struct wiphy *wiphy, u32 changed)
